cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
title: "Open-Source Instrumentation for Reproducible Industrial Wireless Packet Observability in Educational Cyber-Physical Laboratories"
abstract: >-
  An open-source instrumentation and reproducibility workflow for packet-level
  observability in educational cyber-physical laboratories. The artifact provides
  a configuration-driven, software-only synthetic demo mode that generates
  deterministic packet traces, computes packet-level metrics, produces figures,
  and writes per-run manifests with SHA-256 hashes, across four technology-like
  case-study profiles (Wi-Fi-like, BLE/IIoT-like, IEEE 802.15.4/Zigbee-like, and
  LoRa/Sub-GHz/SDR receive-only). It is extensible to owned-device and
  receive-only observation. Synthetic demo-mode outputs are not real radio
  measurements, and the artifact makes no jamming, scheduling, or
  standard-validation claims.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-06-30
license: MIT
keywords:
  - packet observability
  - instrumentation
  - reproducibility
  - educational cyber-physical laboratory
  - synthetic demo mode
  - receive-only SDR
